tui-easy-textinput

Portions of this crate are derived from first-party code in the
xai-ratatui-textarea crate, part of xAI's Grok build (grok-build) project.

Original source:
  Repository: https://github.com/xai-org/grok-build
  Directory:  crates/codegen/xai-ratatui-textarea/src/
  Files vendored (5 files, ~10,944 LoC):
    - textarea.rs          — input widget + TextAreaState carrier
    - editor.rs            — EditBuffer / EditCommand / EditPlan types
    - editor_keys.rs       — keymap dispatch (crossterm-coupled)
    - render/mod.rs        — render submodule facade
    - render/line_utils.rs — render helpers for typed-line cells
  Copyright:  2023-2026 xAI
  License:    Apache License, Version 2.0

Excluded from the vendoring scope (NOT vendored):
  - wrapping.rs    — already vendored into the sibling `tui-easy-wrap`
                     crate (round-2 borrow-and-port). Re-vendoring here
                     would create a workspace circular dependency on
                     `textwrap` via `tui-easy-wrap`'s path-only dep on
                     the same leaf.
  - editor_tests/  — upstream internal test directory; per the rounds
                     6/10/11/12 vendoring pattern, vendored siblings do
                     NOT carry upstream test files. Round-13 tests live
                     in `crates/tui-easy-textinput/src/lib.rs` (inline)
                     and `crates/tui-easy-textinput/tests/textinput_integration.rs`
                     (integration), and target the public re-export
                     surface exclusively.

The vendoring adopts the SAME upstream source as the sibling
`tui-easy-wrap` crate (round-2): the xai-ratatui-textarea crate is the
canonical source for both wrap-algorithms (round-2) and the
input-widget surface (round-13). Cross-reference `crates/tui-easy-wrap/NOTICE`
for the upstream Apache-2.0 attribution precedent (verbatim shape).

The vendored surface is consumed through this crate's thin
`src/lib.rs`, which re-exports the upstream public types (`TextArea`,
`TextAreaState`, `EditBuffer`, `EditCommand`, ...).

See LICENSE-APACHE in this crate for the full license text. The
xai-ratatui-textarea crate does not redistribute any third-party source itself;
its NOTICE file at the upstream repository documents its own dependencies.
